-------------------------------------------------------------
 Ghostty keybinds  ·  Doomslayer  ·  prefix = Ctrl+G

 HOW: press Ctrl+G, RELEASE it, then the action key.
      (Not a chord — same idea as tmux prefix.)

 Ctrl+G ?         command palette (search actions/binds)
 Ctrl+G Ctrl+H    this cheat sheet in less (shell prompt)
 Esc              cancel prefix mode
 CLI:             ghostty +list-keybinds
-------------------------------------------------------------

  PREFIX
    Ctrl+G            enter prefix mode (one shot)
    Esc               cancel prefix mode
    g  or  Ctrl+G     send real Ctrl+G to the app (after prefix)

  TABS  (~ tmux windows)
    Ctrl+G c          new tab
    Ctrl+G n / p      next / previous tab
    Ctrl+G l / 0      last tab
    Ctrl+G 1 … 9      go to tab N
    Ctrl+G ,          rename tab
    Ctrl+G w          tab overview
    Ctrl+G d          close whole tab (all splits in it)

  WINDOWS
    Ctrl+G Shift+c    new window
    Ctrl+G &          close window

  SPLITS  (~ tmux panes)
    Ctrl+G h          horizontal split  (left | right)
    Ctrl+G v          vertical split    (top / bottom)
    Ctrl+G %          same as h
    Ctrl+G "          same as v
    Ctrl+G ←↓↑→       focus split
    Ctrl+G R          resize MODE (then arrows/hjkl; Esc exits)
    Ctrl+G Ctrl+←…→   one-shot resize
    Ctrl+G Shift+hjkl focus split (vim)
    Ctrl+G o / ;      next / previous split
    Ctrl+G z          zoom / unzoom pane
    Ctrl+G =          equalize splits
    Ctrl+G Ctrl+←↓↑→  resize split

  SEARCH / SCROLL
    Ctrl+G f  or  /   start search
    Ctrl+G [ / ]      page up / page down
    Ctrl+G Home / G   scroll top / bottom
    Ctrl+G a          select all

  MISC
    Ctrl+G ?          VIEW KEYBINDS — command palette
    Ctrl+G Ctrl+H     VIEW KEYBINDS — this cheat sheet (less)

    Ctrl+G r          reload config
    Ctrl+G Enter      toggle fullscreen
    Ctrl+G i          terminal inspector

  NOTES
    · Shell Ctrl+D already exits a pane (EOF) — no prefix needed.
    · Prefix+d closes the tab; prefix+& closes the OS window.
    · h/v use tmux naming: h = side-by-side, v = stacked.
